1
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:15,910
MY PHONE

2
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:17,910
IT'S ON MY DESK

3
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:20,370
BRING IT!

4
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:27,290
Kannawa-san?

5
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,160
My phone!

6
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:31,300
I'm tellin' ya to bring it to me!

7
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,260
Y-Y-Yes, ma'am!

8
00:00:41,870 --> 00:00:44,770
Why are you spacing out, Kamegawa?

9
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:47,840
Did Kannawa-senpai get mad at you?

10
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:50,270
Well, that's partially true.

11
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:52,050
Partially?

12
00:00:52,050 --> 00:00:53,280
Oh, no...

13
00:00:53,550 --> 00:00:57,120
I noticed Senpai's dialect slips out 
when she gets flustered.

14
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:58,910
She did it just a bit ago.

15
00:01:00,170 --> 00:01:01,160
Dialect?

16
00:01:01,890 --> 00:01:03,950
Oh! I need to head back.

17
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:06,530
I'll catch you later.

18
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:07,360
Okay.

19
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:12,960
Dialect, huh?

20
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:16,660
I haven't heard her using 
a dialect at all, though.

21
00:01:19,430 --> 00:01:23,100
MY AWKWARD SENPAI

22
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:53,020
EPISODE 7: MOM'S COMIN' TO VISIT!

23
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:51,820
"Mom's Comin' to Visit!"

24
00:03:09,330 --> 00:03:12,460
You've been sighing for a while.

25
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:14,240
Cut it out. It's making me feel down.

26
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:15,750
I-I'm sorry.

27
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:18,760
My parents have been messaging me nonstop,

28
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:21,510
even after I told them 
I can't reply when I'm working.

29
00:03:22,690 --> 00:03:25,970
You're still a kid if you feel annoyed 
about your parents reaching out.

30
00:03:25,970 --> 00:03:27,680
You don't understand what a blessing it is.

31
00:03:28,390 --> 00:03:30,180
You're absolutely right.

32
00:03:31,190 --> 00:03:33,340
<i>I did it again!</i>

33
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:36,420
<i>I could have said that in a nicer way!</i>

34
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:40,190
YU-CHAN

35
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:45,340
Do your parents call you "Yu-chan"?

36
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:54,860
Don't be late to our next meeting,

37
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:55,920
Yu-chan.

38
00:03:57,070 --> 00:03:59,490
I knew you'd say that!

39
00:03:59,490 --> 00:04:00,610
Just messing with you.

40
00:04:00,610 --> 00:04:02,880
You should go visit your family sometime.

41
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:06,350
I guess I could visit this weekend.
I don't have any plans.

42
00:04:06,610 --> 00:04:08,210
Do they live near here?

43
00:04:08,210 --> 00:04:10,020
They live in Kawaguchi City, in Saitama.

44
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:10,850
That's close!

45
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:14,490
Which is why they sometimes 
come to check in on me.

46
00:04:14,490 --> 00:04:17,600
They nag at me to cook my own 
meals or to clean and such.

47
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:19,860
It's not always nice that they live so close.

48
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:23,130
I see. That can be a lot...

49
00:04:23,130 --> 00:04:24,360
Yu-chan.

50
00:04:25,130 --> 00:04:26,370
Hey!

51
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:31,620
<i>That being said...</i>

52
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:35,540
<i>I wouldn't want my parents to 
see me livin' alone like this.</i>

53
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:39,380
I'm glad my hometown's 
all the way in Kyushu.

54
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,880
Time to go shopping.

55
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:46,390
NAKA STREET SHOPPING DISTRICT
BIG BARGAIN SALE

56
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:48,460
<i>I haven't been here in a while.</i>

57
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:50,230
<i>What should I get?</i>

58
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:54,730
WAGYU FAIR

59
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:59,250
<i>That's right! This is what it's all about!</i>

60
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:01,660
<i>I can eat whatever I want, whenever I want!</i>

61
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:04,280
<i>This is the true pleasure of living alone!</i>

62
00:05:07,410 --> 00:05:10,370
LIMITED-TIME SALE! BENTO BOXES

63
00:05:09,130 --> 00:05:10,370
<i>This is it!</i>

64
00:05:11,050 --> 00:05:13,750
<i>It can't be helped, since it's a limited sale.</i>

65
00:05:13,750 --> 00:05:17,270
<i>If they're offerin' such a kindness,
I gotta take advantage of it.</i>

66
00:05:17,270 --> 00:05:19,230
Huh? Kannawa-senpai?

67
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:20,960
What?!

68
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:22,590
What are you doing here?!

69
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:25,090
I come here sometimes, 
since it's in my neighborhood.

70
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:26,810
<i>Shoot!</i>

71
00:05:26,810 --> 00:05:27,840
<i>I forgot!</i>

72
00:05:28,570 --> 00:05:29,590
Senpai?

73
00:05:30,470 --> 00:05:32,130
Wait a minute.

74
00:05:32,130 --> 00:05:34,480
Didn't you say you were 
going to visit your family?

75
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:36,650
I thought I would,

76
00:05:36,650 --> 00:05:38,830
But it turns out they took 
off on vacation today.

77
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:41,980
I didn't know you shopped at this store, too.

78
00:05:41,980 --> 00:05:44,620
Yeah I... Sometimes...

79
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:46,240
What are you shopping for?

80
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:49,430
The veggies here are pretty cheap.

81
00:05:49,430 --> 00:05:51,240
I... I see.

82
00:05:51,550 --> 00:05:52,590
<i>Shoot...</i>

83
00:05:52,590 --> 00:05:55,070
<i>I only came here to buy bento.</i>

84
00:05:55,070 --> 00:05:57,620
<i>He's gonna find out that I don't cook!</i>

85
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,730
Tonight's menu is teriyaki tuna 
and deep-fried eggplant.

86
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:03,090
Oh! Make that one thing, too.

87
00:06:03,090 --> 00:06:04,220
The fluffy thing.

88
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:08,380
You mean the yam okonomiyaki? 
You really do like that stuff.

89
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:11,390
Yeah, I really do. 
I could eat it for every meal.

90
00:06:16,810 --> 00:06:19,320
<i>He looks super jealous of them.</i>

91
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:20,860
<i>Well, of course he does.</i>

92
00:06:21,570 --> 00:06:25,720
<i>Could it be that Senpai 
and I look like a couple?</i>

93
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:28,160
<i>Wait, what am I thinking?</i>

94
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:30,920
Hey, do you...

95
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:33,820
It's admirable that you do your own cooking,

96
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:36,560
but are there times you wish you 
had a girlfriend who's a good cook?

97
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,370
Huh?

98
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:40,330
<i>Why did I just ask that?</i>

99
00:06:40,330 --> 00:06:43,340
Hmm... Well...

100
00:06:43,650 --> 00:06:46,630
Being a good cook <i>is</i> a nice thing.

101
00:06:47,820 --> 00:06:48,760
But...

102
00:06:49,620 --> 00:06:54,140
Being able to cook together,
or if someone who usually never cooks

103
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:57,110
spends time practicing cooking for me...

104
00:06:57,890 --> 00:06:58,850
That would be...

105
00:06:59,230 --> 00:07:02,730
Yeah! That would be nice... I think.

106
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:05,230
Speaking of which...

107
00:07:05,230 --> 00:07:07,760
What did you come to buy, Senpai?

108
00:07:08,670 --> 00:07:10,220
V-Vegetables!

109
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:13,350
Oh! I heard mustard spinach is on sale today.

110
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:13,870
MUSTARD SPINACH SALE

111
00:07:14,450 --> 00:07:15,220
I...

112
00:07:16,190 --> 00:07:17,950
I see...

113
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:24,330
Good work!

114
00:07:24,330 --> 00:07:26,300
TO THE CORPORATION

115
00:07:25,460 --> 00:07:26,300
There.

116
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:27,980
Oh. Good work.

117
00:07:28,570 --> 00:07:32,050
Sorry to dump the meeting 
for the collab café on you.

118
00:07:32,050 --> 00:07:33,640
Did it go well?

119
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:34,750
It did.

120
00:07:34,750 --> 00:07:38,980
We finalized the merchandise lineup,
 as well as the restaurant's layout...

121
00:07:39,850 --> 00:07:41,560
Wait... Senpai!

122
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:43,560
What happened to your hand?!

123
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:45,130
Oh, these?

124
00:07:45,130 --> 00:07:47,420
Th-They're just paper cuts!

125
00:07:47,420 --> 00:07:49,930
Don't worry, I'm fine now.

126
00:07:49,930 --> 00:07:52,420
Is it even possible to 
get that many paper cuts?

127
00:07:53,070 --> 00:07:55,200
MOM

128
00:07:53,750 --> 00:07:55,200
<i>Ugh.</i>

129
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:58,570
<i>I told her not to call me on weekdays!</i>

130
00:07:59,150 --> 00:08:00,640
<i>Just ignore her.</i>

131
00:08:01,930 --> 00:08:05,440
You're still a kid if you feel annoyed 
about your parents reaching out.

132
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,200
You don't understand what a blessing it is.

133
00:08:11,050 --> 00:08:13,410
Sorry, but could you fix this for me?

134
00:08:13,410 --> 00:08:14,970
Huh? Oh... Sure.

135
00:08:13,410 --> 00:08:14,970
Hello?

136
00:08:14,970 --> 00:08:15,970
Hold on.

137
00:08:15,970 --> 00:08:17,990
I'm going somewhere I can talk to you.

138
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,480
Fix this?

139
00:08:21,770 --> 00:08:22,700
Hello.

140
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:25,230
<i>You finally answered, Azusa-chan!</i>

141
00:08:25,550 --> 00:08:28,140
<i>I've called you so many times now.</i>

142
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,080
Yeah, yeah.

143
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,010
<i>Listen.</i>

144
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:35,120
<i>Remember Sayo-chan next door? 
Her grandbaby was born just yesterday!</i>

145
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:39,630
<i>Things seem to be goin' well there, and I just...</i>

146
00:08:40,030 --> 00:08:43,340
I told ya, stop callin' me on my work days!

147
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:45,000
<i>Oh, sorry, dear!</i>

148
00:08:45,350 --> 00:08:48,640
<i>I only wanted to ask ya 
something important, that's all.</i>

149
00:08:49,610 --> 00:08:51,000
Fine. Just one thing.

150
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,190
<i>'Kay!</i>

151
00:08:52,190 --> 00:08:56,010
<i>Are ya by any chance... dating anyone?</i>

152
00:08:56,290 --> 00:08:57,120
What?

153
00:08:57,120 --> 00:09:00,660
<i>Y'know how you asked me to send ya 
a pic of the yukata the other day?</i>

154
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:03,270
<i>That's when my motherly intuition kicked in.</i>

155
00:09:03,270 --> 00:09:05,370
Wh-What's that even mean?

156
00:09:05,370 --> 00:09:08,040
<i>Oh, if you're not, that's fine, too!</i>

157
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:10,600
<i>If push comes to shove, 
arranged marriage is an option.</i>

158
00:09:11,190 --> 00:09:13,630
I have a boyfriend, so there's no need.

159
00:09:13,630 --> 00:09:15,730
<i>Huh?! Wait! You do?!</i>

160
00:09:15,730 --> 00:09:16,840
<i>What's he li—</i>

161
00:09:19,410 --> 00:09:22,870
I-I'm sorry. I didn't mean to eavesdrop...

162
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:26,000
I know you told me to fix this,

163
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,630
but it's still got some ink, so I don't know 
what exactly needs to be fixed...

164
00:09:29,630 --> 00:09:30,580
Huh?

165
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:33,320
No, I wanted you to fix it 
back where it belongs...

166
00:09:34,110 --> 00:09:36,380
Wait. Is "fix" dialect?

167
00:09:38,910 --> 00:09:40,560
Oh! Is that what that was?

168
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:42,390
I'm sorry! I didn't realize.

169
00:09:42,390 --> 00:09:44,220
No, that was on me.

170
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:45,160
I'm sorry.

171
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:47,140
"To fix" means "to put away," so...

172
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:48,960
Oh, it's okay!

173
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:51,970
I sometimes look up your dialect,

174
00:09:51,970 --> 00:09:54,600
but this time I took it too literally.

175
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:56,400
What?

176
00:09:56,400 --> 00:10:00,660
D-Do I speak in my dialect that often?

177
00:10:01,270 --> 00:10:06,730
I was doin' my best to speak in standard 
Japanese to avoid work-related issues...

178
00:10:07,770 --> 00:10:09,970
Could it be that there were 
times something I said

179
00:10:09,970 --> 00:10:12,200
didn't parse well just 'cuz I didn't realize?!

180
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,170
Oh...

181
00:10:13,170 --> 00:10:14,170
So there were?!

182
00:10:14,170 --> 00:10:15,170
N-No, there weren't!

183
00:10:15,930 --> 00:10:17,420
Please don't worry!

184
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:20,030
Sorry...

185
00:10:20,030 --> 00:10:22,380
There were... actually a few.

186
00:10:22,930 --> 00:10:24,600
Figures.

187
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:26,750
Um, Senpai—

188
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:27,870
Kamegawa!

189
00:10:27,870 --> 00:10:28,940
Yes?

190
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:32,100
From now on, if something I say 
doesn't make sense, tell me.

191
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:33,440
Please.

192
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:35,350
Y-Yes, ma'am.

193
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:44,100
<i>The person Senpai's dating...</i>

194
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:50,960
MOM

195
00:10:49,610 --> 00:10:50,960
Again?

196
00:10:52,230 --> 00:10:53,260
Hello?

197
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:54,830
<i>Oh! Azusa-chan!</i>

198
00:10:54,830 --> 00:10:56,460
I told ya, I'm workin'!

199
00:10:56,810 --> 00:10:59,580
<i>I forgot to tell ya an important thing.</i>

200
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:03,240
<i>I'm in front of your house right now.</i>

201
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:04,370
What?!

202
00:11:04,370 --> 00:11:05,220
Huh?!

203
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:07,330
What time are ya off work?

204
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,370
If it's possible, I'm thinkin' 
we can go out to eat

205
00:11:10,370 --> 00:11:13,230
with that boyfriend of yours 
that you mentioned.

206
00:11:13,690 --> 00:11:16,290
<i>Hello? Did ya hear me? Azusa?</i>

207
00:11:17,340 --> 00:11:18,940
What?!

208
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:21,940
Are you all right, Senpai?

209
00:11:23,590 --> 00:11:24,980
My mother appears to be...

210
00:11:25,410 --> 00:11:27,450
at my house.

211
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:29,850
What? Right now?

212
00:11:29,850 --> 00:11:31,210
And she...

213
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:36,510
asked if I could go out to eat 
with her and my boyfriend.

214
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:38,010
Huh?

215
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,150
Th-That's great!

216
00:11:41,150 --> 00:11:42,350
It's not!

217
00:11:43,070 --> 00:11:43,840
I don't...

218
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:44,810
What?

219
00:11:45,460 --> 00:11:49,350
I don't even have a boyfriend.

220
00:11:51,620 --> 00:11:53,300
<i>Why am I relieved?!</i>

221
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:56,110
<i>I'm being so rude!</i>

222
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:59,320
This isn't good...

223
00:12:00,350 --> 00:12:02,490
At this rate, she's going to 
hook me up with a stranger.

224
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:04,740
Um...

225
00:12:05,090 --> 00:12:08,490
What if I pretend to be your boyfriend?

226
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:16,380
Finally finished.

227
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:17,380
Let's go home.

228
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:20,190
Yeah! This week was rough.

229
00:12:20,190 --> 00:12:21,130
Sure was.

230
00:12:22,070 --> 00:12:23,680
Let's do this.

231
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:24,630
Right.

232
00:12:24,630 --> 00:12:26,760
WE ARE COWORKERS

233
00:12:25,510 --> 00:12:26,760
Okay, firstly,

234
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:29,420
our story is that we're coworkers.

235
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:30,360
Got it?

236
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:32,270
Yes, ma'am. Understood.

237
00:12:32,270 --> 00:12:33,930
Also...

238
00:12:33,930 --> 00:12:35,690
What else do we need to decide on?

239
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:37,800
Um...

240
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:40,360
Maybe how long we've been dating?

241
00:12:40,730 --> 00:12:41,940
One week!

242
00:12:43,110 --> 00:12:44,820
That's rather recent.

243
00:12:45,910 --> 00:12:49,080
Well... I don't know much 
about this kind of thing.

244
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:52,170
I mean, I don't know a lot, either.

245
00:12:52,790 --> 00:12:55,040
How about four months?

246
00:12:55,570 --> 00:12:56,830
Why four months?

247
00:12:56,830 --> 00:13:00,830
I was thinking that it's been 
four months since I met you.

248
00:13:01,690 --> 00:13:03,720
<i>Actually, it's been longer than that...</i>

249
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:05,440
I see.

250
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:08,220
A strategy to skillfully blend in the facts.

251
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:09,850
Got it! What else?

252
00:13:09,850 --> 00:13:11,070
Um...

253
00:13:11,070 --> 00:13:13,170
Establishing the scenario is important,

254
00:13:13,170 --> 00:13:16,850
but I actually don't know much about you.

255
00:13:17,650 --> 00:13:20,690
Like your hobbies, or what 
you do on weekends.

256
00:13:20,690 --> 00:13:24,210
I feel like I'd be able to answer 
your mom's questions better

257
00:13:24,210 --> 00:13:26,110
if I knew those kinds of things.

258
00:13:28,090 --> 00:13:29,700
Oh, if it's difficult to say, then—

259
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:31,120
My hobby is gaming.

260
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:32,960
Oh, really?

261
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:34,120
Me, too!

262
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:38,540
I just started playing <i>Final Fantasy VII Rebirth</i>, 
and I'm only in the early stages,

263
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:40,500
but the areas are so vast!

264
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:42,300
I was having fun just exploring,

265
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:44,170
and before I knew it, two hours had passed!

266
00:13:44,170 --> 00:13:45,290
I get you!

267
00:13:45,290 --> 00:13:47,550
I tell myself that I'll work on the main story,

268
00:13:47,550 --> 00:13:50,620
but then I get distracted by all the little 
details and end up straying away.

269
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:52,600
But that's what makes it fun!

270
00:13:53,490 --> 00:13:56,060
We have a hobby in common! Nice!

271
00:13:57,410 --> 00:13:58,490
Yes!

272
00:13:58,810 --> 00:14:01,500
Okay! We can get through the rest somehow!

273
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,770
Yes, ma'am! I'll do my best!

274
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:16,490
Is my tie straight?

275
00:14:16,490 --> 00:14:18,080
Is the color okay?

276
00:14:19,310 --> 00:14:21,130
You're too nervous.

277
00:14:21,130 --> 00:14:22,880
Don't worry about these things.

278
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:24,400
We'll just go as planned.

279
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:26,880
Oh, there you are.

280
00:14:27,690 --> 00:14:30,060
Sorry to keep you two waiting!

281
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:32,470
I-Is she your sister?

282
00:14:32,890 --> 00:14:33,890
She's my mother.

283
00:14:35,340 --> 00:14:36,520
A cousin?

284
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:37,590
My mother!

285
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:40,900
AZUSA'S MOTHER - SAKURA KANNAWA

286
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:40,900
Sorry for inviting you two out so suddenly.

287
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:43,220
You must be Azusa's boyfriend.

288
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:47,920
This is Yu Kamegawa-san. 
He's also my coworker.

289
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,170
I'm Kamegawa!

290
00:14:49,170 --> 00:14:50,910
It's nice to meet you!

291
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:52,780
The pleasure is mine.

292
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:56,420
This is the first time my daughter's 
introduced me to a boyfriend!

293
00:14:56,420 --> 00:14:57,910
I'm so happy.

294
00:15:01,710 --> 00:15:06,050
And then she thought she was real 
mature and ordered the spicy ramen!

295
00:15:06,050 --> 00:15:09,320
She didn't have to finish it, 
but she kept goin' with tears in her eyes.

296
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:10,450
So silly of her!

297
00:15:10,450 --> 00:15:12,180
Hey, Mom!

298
00:15:13,590 --> 00:15:16,680
She's so stubborn, just like her father.

299
00:15:18,790 --> 00:15:19,710
Oh, yeah.

300
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,580
Kamegawa-san!

301
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:24,020
What part about her were you drawn to?

302
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:25,140
What?

303
00:15:25,140 --> 00:15:27,860
Huh?! Don't ask such a weird question!

304
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:29,810
What about it is weird?

305
00:15:29,810 --> 00:15:31,410
He's your boyfriend, right?

306
00:15:31,410 --> 00:15:32,820
I wanna know.

307
00:15:34,270 --> 00:15:37,620
<i>There's no way he can answer that!</i>

308
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:38,430
Senp—

309
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:41,000
Azusa...san...

310
00:15:46,170 --> 00:15:48,510
Sorry, I need to answer this.

311
00:15:48,770 --> 00:15:50,020
It's a client.

312
00:15:50,020 --> 00:15:51,500
Oh, of course.

313
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:56,260
She works so hard.

314
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:58,400
She does.

315
00:16:01,730 --> 00:16:02,570
So?

316
00:16:02,570 --> 00:16:04,570
What's really goin' on between you two?

317
00:16:04,570 --> 00:16:05,200
Huh?

318
00:16:06,150 --> 00:16:09,130
W-Well, um...

319
00:16:09,730 --> 00:16:11,010
'Cuz, you know...

320
00:16:11,010 --> 00:16:13,870
She's good-looking, right?

321
00:16:13,870 --> 00:16:15,640
Y-Yes.

322
00:16:16,030 --> 00:16:17,860
I'm worried about her.

323
00:16:17,860 --> 00:16:21,360
Since she's such an introvert, 
what if she's gettin' scammed out there?

324
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:25,010
Oh, I highly doubt she is...

325
00:16:25,010 --> 00:16:26,190
Really?

326
00:16:26,190 --> 00:16:29,200
You're not thinkin' of 
swindlin' her or anything?

327
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,380
I'm not!

328
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:34,260
She's only really interested in games.

329
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:36,280
I'm sure she has money because of that.

330
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:38,180
Um... I said I'm not interested in that.

331
00:16:38,930 --> 00:16:41,410
Could it be that you two have a child?!

332
00:16:41,410 --> 00:16:42,500
We don't!

333
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:44,190
We really don't! We're fine!

334
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:46,530
Oh, of course!

335
00:16:46,530 --> 00:16:48,530
You two have that feelin' about ya.

336
00:16:48,530 --> 00:16:49,690
You're so quick to shift gears!

337
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:52,030
Sorry.

338
00:16:52,030 --> 00:16:55,170
I just can't help it, knowin' how she is.

339
00:16:55,170 --> 00:16:59,120
I bet she's tough on the folks 
around her at work, too, right?

340
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:02,120
Huh? Well, uh...

341
00:17:05,580 --> 00:17:11,880
When she was a kid, she was 
simply a shy, reserved girl.

342
00:17:13,060 --> 00:17:14,750
In elementary school,

343
00:17:14,750 --> 00:17:18,850
she was elected to be the class 
representative for her good grades.

344
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:22,160
She did the best she could in her own way,

345
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:25,850
but nothing can be that easy.

346
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:30,290
During practice for sports day,

347
00:17:30,290 --> 00:17:33,340
one of her classmates got hurt 
while messin' around.

348
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:38,680
She felt responsible for not doin' a good job,

349
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:43,290
and she ended up yellin', 
"Calm down!" to everyone.

350
00:17:43,670 --> 00:17:47,720
From then on, everyone around 
her was scared of her.

351
00:17:48,290 --> 00:17:50,180
But that got me thinkin'.

352
00:17:50,180 --> 00:17:52,530
That awkward girl...

353
00:17:52,530 --> 00:17:55,800
It's her unrelenting kindness that made her
determined to protect her classmates,

354
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:58,730
even at the cost of them hatin' her.

355
00:17:58,730 --> 00:18:03,380
I guess it's hard to understand 
where I'm coming from.

356
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:07,310
I know she should be more 
put-together at her age,

357
00:18:07,780 --> 00:18:09,170
but please don't hate her.

358
00:18:09,170 --> 00:18:09,940
I don't.

359
00:18:11,100 --> 00:18:14,690
There's no way I would ever hate Senpai.

360
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:19,920
It's true that her words can be harsh,

361
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:23,700
and that there are people 
around her who say she's scary.

362
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:29,330
But she's only doing that to warn me 
before I can mess anything up.

363
00:18:29,630 --> 00:18:32,190
And if I do things correctly, 
she makes sure to praise me.

364
00:18:32,190 --> 00:18:36,970
I know that at the end of it all, 
she's a genuinely kind person.

365
00:18:36,970 --> 00:18:38,880
You're so sweet!

366
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:41,460
Now I'm feeling all happy!

367
00:18:41,810 --> 00:18:42,970
Just the other day she...

368
00:18:44,270 --> 00:18:45,900
Thank you...

369
00:18:52,670 --> 00:18:55,680
Sorry to keep you until this hour,

370
00:18:55,680 --> 00:18:57,970
but I had a lot of fun.

371
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:00,090
No, no. The pleasure's mine.

372
00:19:00,090 --> 00:19:01,990
Oh, that's right.

373
00:19:02,650 --> 00:19:06,370
Thanks for playing along for her sake.

374
00:19:06,370 --> 00:19:07,180
Huh?

375
00:19:07,670 --> 00:19:10,120
You're not really her boyfriend, are you?

376
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:12,380
Uh, well...

377
00:19:12,380 --> 00:19:16,820
You called Azusa "Senpai," after all.

378
00:19:18,870 --> 00:19:19,800
Still...

379
00:19:20,570 --> 00:19:25,870
I'm relieved to know she has someone 
as responsible as you by her side.

380
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:28,280
Not at all!

381
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:31,080
I need to do better at my job.

382
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:34,830
Even today, I couldn't understand 
Senpai's dialect—I mean, vocabulary—

383
00:19:34,830 --> 00:19:36,580
and caused problems...

384
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:37,280
Huh?

385
00:19:38,310 --> 00:19:39,660
Mom!

386
00:19:39,660 --> 00:19:41,530
The taxi's here.

387
00:19:41,530 --> 00:19:43,010
Coming!

388
00:19:43,010 --> 00:19:44,390
One more thing.

389
00:19:57,660 --> 00:19:58,840
Sorry for the hold-up!

390
00:19:59,180 --> 00:20:01,650
Get back home safely.

391
00:20:01,650 --> 00:20:03,550
Yeah. See you tomorrow.

392
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:20,060
Now, eat up.

393
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:22,350
It's to thank you for 
sticking with me yesterday.

394
00:20:22,350 --> 00:20:24,080
Thank you so much!

395
00:20:24,080 --> 00:20:25,110
Let's eat!

396
00:20:27,770 --> 00:20:29,150
Thank you for waiting.

397
00:20:29,150 --> 00:20:31,120
Here is the pasta lunch.

398
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:36,000
I can't cut this.

399
00:20:39,390 --> 00:20:43,060
If it's okay with you, can I have that?

400
00:20:43,060 --> 00:20:43,670
Huh?

401
00:20:44,430 --> 00:20:47,510
Oh... Do you like tomatoes?

402
00:20:47,840 --> 00:20:50,570
Oh, well... as much as anyone, I guess...

403
00:20:50,570 --> 00:20:52,840
I mean, yes! I do!

404
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:53,890
They're my favorite.

405
00:20:56,650 --> 00:20:58,360
Um, sorry.

406
00:20:58,700 --> 00:21:04,350
When you say "cut," it means 
"eat" in the Kyushu dialect, right?

407
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:08,340
So "I can't cut" means "I can't eat..."

408
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:11,490
In other words, you don't like tomatoes.

409
00:21:12,610 --> 00:21:13,900
How did you—

410
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:15,700
You're too well-versed in that dialect!

411
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:16,890
Not at all.

412
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:20,610
Your Kyushu dialect is hard to study

413
00:21:20,610 --> 00:21:22,750
since it's mixed with other 
dialects from that area.

414
00:21:24,190 --> 00:21:26,300
A-Anyway!

415
00:21:26,300 --> 00:21:29,000
What did you talk to my
mother about yesterday?

416
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:29,510
Huh?

417
00:21:29,840 --> 00:21:32,800
During our ride home, she kept 
trying to dig up information on you.

418
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,520
It was a lot to handle!

419
00:21:35,340 --> 00:21:36,980
W-Well...

420
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:42,940
The fact that she speaks to you in 
our dialect must mean she trusts ya.

421
00:21:47,620 --> 00:21:51,240
We didn't... talk about anything much.

422
00:21:51,550 --> 00:21:54,080
What's with that face? You're lying!

423
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:57,050
You think it's okay to lie 
to your mentor like that?!

424
00:21:57,050 --> 00:21:58,980
Well, then, it's a secret.

425
00:21:58,980 --> 00:22:01,560
What?! That's even more unforgivable!

426
00:22:01,560 --> 00:22:02,850
Come on, now...

427
00:22:02,850 --> 00:22:05,510
Oh, it looks like we get a drink after our meal.

428
00:22:05,510 --> 00:22:08,590
Don't change the subject!

